    {
      "at": "2026-11-13T15:20:58Z",
      "choice": "applied",
      "earlier": [],
      "finding": "R1-F1",
      "reason": "Repair is now only for themes added to an otherwise unchanged set: status says a full build is needed and repair refuses, even when told to go on, if a linked theme changed or went or the vectors model, dimension or prefix differs; the outcome, criterion 4, the tests, the breaks and the deferred work say so."
    },
    {
      "at": "2026-11-13T15:26:23Z",
      "choice": "applied",
      "earlier": [],
      "finding": "R2-F1",
      "reason": "The median and the three band edges are now exact order statistics found in bounded memory by two passes, not a histogram estimate; a pair exactly at the median is not linked; the tests compare with numpy median and quantile and use values within 0.0005 of the median and the edges; the breaks include a coarse histogram and a missing interpolation."
    },
    {
      "at": "2026-11-13T15:27:29Z",
      "choice": "applied",
      "earlier": [],
      "finding": "R3-F1",
      "reason": "The exact selection no longer collects the values of a bin: the closeness is an integer in billionths and a radix selection over the blocks pins the rank in at most two passes with memory fixed by the bins whatever the spread, equal values being counts; tests with every pair equal and every pair within 1e-6 check the exact values and that the largest array does not grow with the number of themes; the breaks include collecting a bin whole."
    },
    {
      "at": "2026-11-13T15:32:30Z",
      "choice": "applied",
      "earlier": [],
      "finding": "R4-F1",
      "reason": "The weave now records every theme it processed, with its generation and hashes and its number of links, those with none included; unlinked means not processed, themes with no link are counted separately and never make a repair due; the criterion, the file, the build output, the status tests and the breaks say so, and so does the spec line on the generation of each theme."
    }
  ],
